    {
      "date": "2026-07-02",
      "description": "Gas prices drop ahead of Independence Day travel, offering consumer relief.",
      "details": "The national average for a gallon of regular gasoline decreased by nearly 50 cents from the previous month, reaching $3.83. This reduction in fuel costs provided consumers with some financial relief just before the busy Independence Day travel weekend. Lower gas prices typically free up discretionary income, potentially leading to increased consumer spending on non-essential items. This could explain the positive ROAS and lower CPA for Gardner's Wisconsin Cheese.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "boosts_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "AAA Newsroom"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-04",
      "description": "Independence Day celebrations shift consumer focus offline.",
      "details": "Independence Day is a major federal holiday in the United States, characterized by family gatherings, outdoor activities, fireworks, and travel. Consumer attention typically shifts away from online shopping and digital media during such widespread national celebrations. This holiday effect often results in a significant drop in online conversion intent, even if ad impressions are served. For a DTC food gifting brand, this would likely suppress ROAS and increase CPA.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "seasonal",
      "icon": "🗓️",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "high",
      "source": "US Federal Holiday"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-04",
      "description": "Tour de France 2026 kicks off, capturing global sports attention.",
      "details": "The 113th edition of the Tour de France, a major international cycling event, commenced on July 4th in Barcelona, Spain, running until July 26th. While not a primary US event, major global sporting events can still capture significant attention from sports enthusiasts in the US, potentially diverting social media feed engagement. For a niche brand, this might have a minor impact on feed domination, but likely neutral for spending mood.",
      "intensity": 1,
      "category": "feed",
      "icon": "📱",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "Tour de France Official"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-09",
      "description": "Gas prices reverse course, begin rising again across the US.",
      "details": "After a brief dip, the national average for a gallon of regular gasoline increased by 5 cents overnight to $3.84, with prices continuing to climb due to uncertainty in global crude oil markets. Rising gas prices typically lead to increased financial anxiety among consumers, as a larger portion of their budget is allocated to fuel. This can suppress discretionary spending, including on premium food items.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "AAA Newsroom, LendingTree"
    },
    {
